<!--
    structmerge: two functions that read overlapping-but-different parts of one
    record get ONE synthesized structure carrying both readers' fields, instead
    of a record each carrying only its own.

    Source shape (hand-assembled, no prologue, so each parameter arrives in RDI
    with nothing declaring its type). Every function loads the word at offset 0
    and dereferences it, so offset 0 is a pointer with a pointee, the typed
    claim the merge rule asks for, and adds the 8-byte word at offset 8.

        long off_a(void *p) {             // @0x100000  {0: uchar *, 8, 0x20}
            return *(unsigned char *)*(void **)p
                 + *(long *)((char *)p + 8) + *(long *)((char *)p + 0x20);
        }
        long off_b(void *p) {             // @0x100020  {0: uchar *, 8, 0x14}
            return *(unsigned char *)*(void **)p
                 + *(long *)((char *)p + 8) + *(int *)((char *)p + 0x14);
        }
        long on_a(void *p) {              // @0x100040  {0: int *, 8, 0x20}
            return *(int *)*(void **)p
                 + *(long *)((char *)p + 8) + *(long *)((char *)p + 0x20);
        }
        long on_b(void *p) {              // @0x100060  {0: int *, 8, 0x18}
            return *(int *)*(void **)p
                 + *(long *)((char *)p + 8) + *(long *)((char *)p + 0x18);
        }

        off_a                              off_b
        48 8b 07     mov rax,[rdi]         48 8b 07     mov rax,[rdi]
        0f b6 00     movzx eax,[rax]       0f b6 00     movzx eax,[rax]
        48 8b 57 08  mov rdx,[rdi+8]       48 8b 57 08  mov rdx,[rdi+8]
        48 01 d0     add rax,rdx           48 01 d0     add rax,rdx
        48 8b 57 20  mov rdx,[rdi+0x20]    8b 57 14     mov edx,[rdi+0x14]
        48 01 d0     add rax,rdx           48 01 d0     add rax,rdx
        c3           ret                   c3           ret

    `on_a` and `on_b` are the same two functions with a four-byte load through
    the pointer at offset 0 (`8b 00` for `0f b6 00`), so their offset-0 field is
    a different type and neither of the first pair's records can answer them.

    The two pairs are the two arms of the same experiment. `off_a`/`off_b` run
    with `option structmerge off`: neither layout contains the other, so each
    reader mints a record of its own and re-deciding `off_a` changes nothing.
    `on_a`/`on_b` run with `option structmerge siblings`: they agree about
    offsets 0 and 8, one of the two agreeing claims is a pointer with a pointee,
    so the union of the two layouts is minted, `on_a`'s own record is superseded
    by it, and re-deciding `on_a` answers with the union, the one record both
    readers name.
-->
